WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:11.180
What’s crackin, B? This week we gettin straight absurd with The Stranger by Albert Camus.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.080
My man Meursault ain’t trippin bout
the fact that his mama just died.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.980
Matter of fact, this thug don’t seem to
get bent over much of anything.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:27.480
Meursault slides over to the beach where he hollas at some fox he knew from back-when named Marie.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.040
Even though his mama only been stiff for twenty-fo,

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:35.300
Meursault don’t waste no time slippin Marie
his French baguette. Know what I’m sayin?

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.400
Later she ask if he wanna get
married. And he all like,

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.160
“For sure baby. If you want.
Not like dem cuffs mean nuthin.”

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.440
Man, you sure pimpin ain’t easy?

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:48.420
For a lil while now, Meursault
been chillin with some mack-daddy named Raymond.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:51.000
Thinkin his woman been
actin a hoochie behind his back,

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.880
Ray-Ray gives her five across the face
and brings the law down on his ass.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:01.140
With Meursault’s help, though, Ray-Ray
shakes off the 5-0 and gets off scot-free.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:06.440
Thing is, the bro of Rad-diddy’s fine
lil peach jonezin for some STREET justice.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:12.200
He and his Arab posse roll up on Ray-Ray, 
whip out their shiv, and shank him real good.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:16.780
Later, Meursault rolls up on one of those A-rabs, takes a good long look at his piece,

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:20.880
and realize that whether
he shoot or not, it don’t make a difference.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:26.340
And once the sun’s hot- ass rays start doggin our man, he whips out his glock and POP POP —

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:27.840
Fool gets smoked.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:31.960
Meursault gets thrown in the clink,
and the law puts his ass on death row.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:34.620
But it ain’t only cuz he 187ed a fool.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:40.360
His realest crime is bein a stranger to the rules of society and not havin a heart like errybody else.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:43.060
Before Meursault bout to get tooken out fo good,

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:47.260
a chaplain drops in to give him one last chance to embrace the big G-man.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:51.720
All the sudden — Meursault snaps, get all in the preacher man grill, and say

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:58.580
“Look, bitch. Nothing matters. I did some things in life. I didn’t do other things. And none of it matters.”

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:04.980
Right before he bout to snuff it, our boy finds a lil peace in knowing for sure that it's all bout to end.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:08.040
And the universe ain’t even gonna blink.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.760
Damn man. This cat don’t seem to
give a sh*t bout nothing.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:21.540
If a muthaf**kin meteor dropped down instantly icing a million homies, this fool wouldn’t bat an eye.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:24.560
But does him bein this hard make him a bad dude?

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.740
Truth is, he ain’t bad or good. He
just different from the rest of us.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:33.540
Day in day out, yo regular erryday hood
ain’t got the nuts to tussle with the truth:

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:40.340
Life is meaningless, and what we do or don't do, what does or doesn't happen to us — none of it matters.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.840
When we start bitchin and moanin bout
 how good or bad somethin be,

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.640
we really just imposin order where it don't belong.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:51.800
And when a homie who don’t play dat game swangs in to town, he a stranger to errybody.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:57.620
But even though ain’t nothin seem to bother this hustla, a death sentence can trip up even the hardest of hoods.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:00.920
When Meursault starts marinating on
 meetin the man upstairs,

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:03.620
he flips sh*t bout how these fools gonna ghost him.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:09.460
To Meursault, the worst part bout it is that there ain't no chance he gonna duck the reaper.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:15.280
"All I care about right now is escaping the machinery of justice, seeing if there is any way out of the inevitable...

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:20.800
What really counted was the possibility of escape, a leap to freedom, out of the implacable ritual,

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:26.120
a wild run for it that would give whatever chance for hope there was."

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:32.680
And if you packin a big literary d*ck, you know that my main man Dostoevsky droppin dat same angst in The Idiot:

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:37.960
"But here I should imagine the most terrible part of the [guillotine] is, not the bodily pain at all—

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:42.440
but the certain knowledge that...your soul must quit your body and that you will not longer be a man—

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:48.140
and that this is certain, certain! That's the point—&nbsp;the certainty of it."

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:52.260
What Meursault don't realize till
the end is that hopin to escape the machine

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:57.760
ain't no different than all those other bullsh*t lies that wankstas tell themselves on the reg.

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:03.620
There's only one way to roll like a big dog
 in an indifferent world: with one hand on yo nuts.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:07.700
Embrace that you ain't gonna escape a damned thing, especially death.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:13.280
And when yo time comes to dive six feet
deep, ain't nobody gonna give a damn.

00:04:13.289 --> 00:04:19.020
Cept me, padna! Cuz I want you to take yo hands off your nuts and hit dat subscribe button.

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:21.420
See you next week.
Peace.

